<!--
  ==========================================================================
  AUTOUNATTEND — the birth certificate of an Enclave workstation
  ==========================================================================
  "Do what thou wilt shall be the whole of the Law."
    An attended install is a negotiation conducted at a keyboard, one
    prompt at a time, and negotiations of that shape are lost by
    inches. This file moves the negotiation to paper, where this
    house does its thinking (Bootstrap §II).

  Authorship attributed exclusively to Johnathan "Qasparr" Monroe
  (Greek, -ARR, All Rights Reserved, Without Prejudice).
  XVI day of November, Dies Lunae, Sol in Scorpio, Anno V:xii e.n.
  (2026 e.v.). Method of Science, Aim of Religion. 93.

  WHAT THIS FILE RULES, AND ITS SOURCES:
    * Architecture ARM64; the image installed is selected BY NAME as
      "Windows 11 Pro for Workstations" (Bootstrap §II.2). MEDIA GATE:
      if the verified image in hand carries the edition under another
      name or index, verify with DISM /Get-WimInfo against the actual
      media and correct the /IMAGE/NAME value below before building —
      the answer file selects the edition the media PROVES it holds,
      never the edition a memory insists on.
    * ONE local administrator, and no Microsoft account at any point;
      the OOBE account and network gates are suppressed in the file
      itself (Bootstrap §II.1). This house's machines do not phone
      home to be born.
    * NO CREDENTIAL STANDS IN THIS FILE. The local account is created
      without a password value by design: a password written into an
      answer file is a password published to everyone who ever reads
      the media. The operator sets the account's password at first
      logon, in person, before the machine is trusted — and the
      BitLocker recovery protector is struck in that same first
      session (Bootstrap §II.4 / §IV), its material printed and held
      offline under the founder's hand, never escrowed to a vendor.
    * Locale en-US, time zone America/Detroit (named here in the
      Windows form "Eastern Standard Time", which is Detroit's seat).
    * The disk layout follows Draft §IV and Bootstrap §II.3, sized
      for iron of 1 TiB or more; on smaller iron Windows Setup fails
      rather than improvising — fail-closed is the correct behaviour,
      and the operator re-sizes this file deliberately, on paper.
  ==========================================================================
-->
<unattend xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:unattend">

  <!-- ============================ windowsPE ============================ -->
  <settings pass="windowsPE">

    <!-- Locale for Setup itself and for the image being laid down. -->
    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-International-Core-WinPE"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">
      <SetupUILanguage>
        <UILanguage>en-US</UILanguage>
      </SetupUILanguage>
      <InputLocale>en-US</InputLocale>
      <SystemLocale>en-US</SystemLocale>
      <UILanguage>en-US</UILanguage>
      <UserLocale>en-US</UserLocale>
    </component>

    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-Setup"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">

      <!--
        THE DISK, per Draft §IV / Bootstrap §II.3 (GPT, UEFI iron):
          P1 SYSTEM       260 MiB  FAT32   the EFI seat
          P2 (MSR)         16 MiB  —       Microsoft reserved
          P3 WINDOWS      300 GiB  NTFS    the Windows seat (install target)
          P4 BRIDGE        64 GiB  exFAT   the corridor both boots read
                                           (Portability Law, Amendment VIII)
          P5 POOLRESERVE  512 GiB  RAW     reserved unformatted at birth;
                                           the pooled-storage ceremony of
                                           Bootstrap §III.3 takes it up
                                           post-install. The ReFS EXPANSION
                                           seat (Amendment VII) governs the
                                           pool volumes struck there; no
                                           volume is laid down in ReFS by
                                           this file.
          P6 (reserve)    rest     RAW     the second boot's ground
                                           (Ubuntu, the root host), reserved,
                                           unformatted, and UNTOUCHED by this
                                           bootstrap: Windows is installed
                                           first for the TPM's sake, not
                                           because it owns the disk.
      -->
      <DiskConfiguration>
        <WillShowUI>OnError</WillShowUI>
        <Disk wcm:action="add" xmlns:wcm="http://schemas.microsoft.com/WMIConfig/2002/State">
          <DiskID>0</DiskID>
          <WillWipeDisk>true</WillWipeDisk>
          <CreatePartitions>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>1</Order><Type>EFI</Type><Size>260</Size>
            </CreatePartition>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>2</Order><Type>MSR</Type><Size>16</Size>
            </CreatePartition>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>3</Order><Type>Primary</Type><Size>307200</Size>
            </CreatePartition>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>4</Order><Type>Primary</Type><Size>65536</Size>
            </CreatePartition>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>5</Order><Type>Primary</Type><Size>524288</Size>
            </CreatePartition>
            <CreatePartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>6</Order><Type>Primary</Type><Extend>true</Extend>
            </CreatePartition>
          </CreatePartitions>
          <ModifyPartitions>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>1</Order><PartitionID>1</PartitionID>
              <Format>FAT32</Format><Label>SYSTEM</Label>
            </ModifyPartition>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>2</Order><PartitionID>2</PartitionID>
            </ModifyPartition>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>3</Order><PartitionID>3</PartitionID>
              <Format>NTFS</Format><Label>WINDOWS</Label><Letter>C</Letter>
            </ModifyPartition>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>4</Order><PartitionID>4</PartitionID>
              <Format>exFAT</Format><Label>BRIDGE</Label><Letter>D</Letter>
            </ModifyPartition>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>5</Order><PartitionID>5</PartitionID>
            </ModifyPartition>
            <ModifyPartition wcm:action="add">
              <Order>6</Order><PartitionID>6</PartitionID>
            </ModifyPartition>
          </ModifyPartitions>
        </Disk>
      </DiskConfiguration>

      <!-- The edition, selected by the name the verified image proves. -->
      <ImageInstall>
        <OSImage>
          <InstallFrom>
            <MetaData wcm:action="add" xmlns:wcm="http://schemas.microsoft.com/WMIConfig/2002/State">
              <Key>/IMAGE/NAME</Key>
              <Value>Windows 11 Pro for Workstations</Value>
            </MetaData>
          </InstallFrom>
          <InstallTo>
            <DiskID>0</DiskID>
            <PartitionID>3</PartitionID>
          </InstallTo>
          <WillShowUI>OnError</WillShowUI>
        </OSImage>
      </ImageInstall>

      <!-- No product key stands in this file. The operator's lawful key
           is entered post-install, in person (Bootstrap §I/§II law:
           credentials are never carried on birth media). -->
      <UserData>
        <AcceptEula>true</AcceptEula>
        <FullName>Johnathan Monroe</FullName>
      </UserData>
    </component>
  </settings>

  <!-- ============================ specialize =========================== -->
  <settings pass="specialize">
    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-International-Core"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">
      <InputLocale>en-US</InputLocale>
      <SystemLocale>en-US</SystemLocale>
      <UILanguage>en-US</UILanguage>
      <UserLocale>en-US</UserLocale>
    </component>
    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-Shell-Setup"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">
      <ComputerName>ENCLAVE-WS1</ComputerName>
      <!-- Windows names Detroit's zone "Eastern Standard Time". -->
      <TimeZone>Eastern Standard Time</TimeZone>
      <RegisteredOwner>Johnathan 'Qasparr' Monroe</RegisteredOwner>
    </component>
  </settings>

  <!-- ============================ oobeSystem =========================== -->
  <settings pass="oobeSystem">
    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-International-Core"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">
      <InputLocale>en-US</InputLocale>
      <SystemLocale>en-US</SystemLocale>
      <UILanguage>en-US</UILanguage>
      <UserLocale>en-US</UserLocale>
    </component>

    <component name="Microsoft-Windows-Shell-Setup"
               processorArchitecture="arm64" publicKeyToken="31bf3856ad364e35"
               language="neutral" versionScope="nonSxS">
      <OOBE>
        <HideEULAPage>true</HideEULAPage>
        <HideOEMRegistrationScreen>true</HideOEMRegistrationScreen>
        <!-- The account gates, refused in the file itself: no online
             account is offered, and no wireless courtship delays a
             birth this house has already negotiated on paper. -->
        <HideOnlineAccountScreens>true</HideOnlineAccountScreens>
        <HideWirelessSetupInOOBE>true</HideWirelessSetupInOOBE>
        <NetworkLocation>Home</NetworkLocation>
        <ProtectYourPC>3</ProtectYourPC>
      </OOBE>

      <!-- ONE local administrator. No Password element stands here —
           see the header: credentials are never carried on media.
           The operator sets the password at first logon, in person. -->
      <UserAccounts>
        <LocalAccounts>
          <LocalAccount wcm:action="add" xmlns:wcm="http://schemas.microsoft.com/WMIConfig/2002/State">
            <Name>Qasparr</Name>
            <DisplayName>Johnathan 'Qasparr' Monroe</DisplayName>
            <Group>Administrators</Group>
            <Description>The founder's local administrator — the only account this file creates.</Description>
          </LocalAccount>
        </LocalAccounts>
      </UserAccounts>

      <!-- First logon: the TPM is sealed before any other configuration
           (Bootstrap §II.4 — Windows first wakes the TPM). This command
           strikes the TPM protector; the RECOVERY protector is struck
           by the operator in the same session and its material held
           offline (Bootstrap §II.4/§IV) — deliberately NOT automated
           here, because an automated recovery key is a written-down
           recovery key, and this file is read by the media it rides. -->
      <FirstLogonCommands>
        <SynchronousCommand wcm:action="add" xmlns:wcm="http://schemas.microsoft.com/WMIConfig/2002/State">
          <Order>1</Order>
          <CommandLine>powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "Enable-BitLocker -MountPoint 'C:' -EncryptionMethod XtsAes256 -TpmProtector"</CommandLine>
          <Description>Seal BitLocker to the TPM (Bootstrap §II.4). Then, in this same session: set the account password and strike the BitLocker recovery protector to offline keeping.</Description>
          <RequiresUserInput>false</RequiresUserInput>
        </SynchronousCommand>
      </FirstLogonCommands>
    </component>
  </settings>

  <!--
    ==========================================================================
    Inputs:  the verified Windows 11 ARM64 image (Bootstrap §I).
    Processes: windowsPE lays the disk and the edition; specialize
      names and times the machine; oobeSystem births exactly one
      local administrator and seals BitLocker to the TPM.
    Outputs: a workstation born local, measured, and encrypted —
      no vendor account, no credential on media, the pool ground
      reserved and the second boot's ground untouched.
    Tolerances: edition selection is by the name the media PROVES;
      the layout is sized for iron of 1 TiB or more and fails
      closed on smaller iron rather than improvising.
    93 — Live, Love, and let Love, Live.
    ==========================================================================
  -->
</unattend>
